The decoder's caps with their types as GTypes, not as the number 24
(G_TYPE_INT's value) in an int: gst_caps_new_simple() reads a GType
(64 bits on arm64) from the arguments, got garbage in its upper half and
nsv-decoder-service crashed on the first tone (SIGSEGV in
g_type_value_table_peek). And GStreamer 1.0's format in place of 0.10's
width and depth.

--- a/src/nsv-decoder-task.c
+++ b/src/nsv-decoder-task.c
@@ -472,11 +472,12 @@
 
   gst_bin_add(GST_BIN(priv->pipeline), encoder_bin);
 
+  /* 16 bit mono at 48 kHz, in GStreamer 1.0's terms (0.10's width and
+   * depth are the format now) */
   caps = gst_caps_new_simple("audio/x-raw",
-                             "rate", 24, 48000,
-                             "width", 24, 16,
-                             "depth", 24, 16,
-                             "channels", 24, 1,
+                             "format", G_TYPE_STRING, "S16LE",
+                             "rate", G_TYPE_INT, 48000,
+                             "channels", G_TYPE_INT, 1,
                              NULL);
 
   g_object_set(G_OBJECT(capsfilter), "caps", caps, NULL);
